# L §4.3 rule 1 (round 14): a def states at when it "reads anything law-dated (an input, band, def or rule whose value
# can change with the law date: one with a row or version whose span isn't always, other than an input keyed by one
# period index, which is read at its key's period, §4.6 step 1)". pay is keyed by months, its row in a version governing
# 2026..: double reads it with no at and loads; pay[2026-03] = 100.00 PLN, double = 200.00 PLN. (Writer 6's exemption,
# round 14's U-7, now stated for defs too.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input pay[m in months]: money PLN

def double[m in months]: money PLN = pay[m] + pay[m]

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  pay[*] = 100.00 PLN

ask q1: pay[2026-03]
ask q2: double[2026-03]
=== expect
q1: 100.00 PLN
  cut 2026-12-31
q2: 200.00 PLN
  cut 2026-12-31
